# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. Phase 10 is complete. See [docs/phase-10.md](docs/phase-10.md). Further feature work waits for a new phase document under `docs/`.

Do feature work on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 10 delivered a jurisdiction transfer adapter, Queensland profile fields, generated and stored application PDFs, admin review of an offline signed pack, and manual Fisheries Queensland tracking. Do not add live e-sign, an FQ API, live Stripe keys, seller bank payouts, refund/chargeback workflows, or other jurisdictions’ real processes unless a new phase document asks for that work. Never trust the browser for payment status, bid time, quota availability, or transfer outcome. Never delete quota ledger rows.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture.

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Stop at the end of each phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
